  <data name="label4.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When converting from another software, payments are left unallocated.  This tool is run during a final conversion to allocate all payments to family members.  If the family has a credit balance, then excess payments will be left unallocated.  Payments after the Transfer Date are not usually an issue because this is part of a conversion.  This tool performs an income transfer for every family.  This process can take a long time.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="checkChangedSinceDate.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Only process families with changes since the Changed Since Date.  
Ignores families if financial data has not changed since the date picked.
Designed for bi-weekly usage. NOT for normal users. NOT for conversions.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="label11.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This tool will recreate all of the non-income transfer payment splits in the database with explicitly linked payment splits. The payment dates and amounts will not change, just how the amount is split up between outstanding production. Payment splits will be made to unearned if there is no more outstanding production to explicitly link to.</value>
  </data>
  <metadata name="timerOutput.TrayLocation" type="System.Drawing.Point, System.Drawing, Version=4.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=b03f5f7f11d50a3a">
    <value>17, 17</value>
  </metadata>
  <data name="label1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This tool will convert all insurance overpayments into patient payments (all claims, not just claims with no procedures). Supplemental claimprocs for overpayment amounts will be created to remove claims from insurance overpaid reports. New payments, split to unearned, will be created to allow the insurance overpayments to be treated as patient payments.</value>
  </data>
